Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Tighten pdecobj parent-class lookup and rename object_dec local to result
License: expat

Two cleanups in the class-declaration parser:

- The original parent-class lookup eagerly downcasts `tt.def` to
  `tobjectdef` *before* checking that the def actually has
  `deftype = objectdef`. The downcast on a wrong-typed def is
  technically OK in Pascal (it's just a typed-pointer reinterpretation)
  but the surrounding error path then references the downcast pointer
  via `childof.typename` even when `childof` was set from a non-class
  def. Restructure so the downcast only happens after the deftype check
  and the error message reads from `tt.def.typename` directly.

- The function's own name `object_dec` was being assigned to set its
  result. Rewrite as `result := aktclass;` to match the rest of the
  bootstrap subset's idiom.

--- a/compiler/pdecobj.pas
+++ b/compiler/pdecobj.pas
@@ -386,12 +386,14 @@
            if try_to_consume(_LKLAMMER) then
              begin
                 id_type(tt,false);
-                childof:=tobjectdef(tt.def);
-                if (not assigned(childof)) or
-                   (childof.deftype<>objectdef) then
+                if assigned(tt.def) and (tt.def.deftype=objectdef) then
+                  childof:=tobjectdef(tt.def)
+                else
+                  childof:=nil;
+                if not assigned(childof) then
                  begin
-                   if assigned(childof) then
-                     Message1(type_e_class_type_expected,childof.typename);
+                   if assigned(tt.def) then
+                     Message1(type_e_class_type_expected,tt.def.typename);
                    childof:=nil;
                    aktclass:=tobjectdef.create(classtype,n,nil);
                  end
@@ -756,7 +758,7 @@
         aktobjectdef:=nil;
         current_object_option:=old_object_option;

-         object_dec:=aktclass;
+         result:=aktclass;
       end;

 end.
